On Fri, Jan 2, 2015 at 1:18 PM, guskant <gusni.kantu@gmail.com> wrote:

>
>  OK, so we have the idea as follows:
> 1. add an apostrophe between Cg and V if it does not produce a conflict
> between existing words and if it does not transform the word into lujvo;
> 2. among the other words, if the word is fu'ivla and if it includes CgV
> not in the first syllable, make the glide letter double;
> 3. What to do for the other words (fu'ivla with CgV in the first syllable,
> and possibly some ma'ovla to which process 1 cannot be applied) ?
>

There were only four words that couldn't be adapted by at least one of
those two methods when this was discussed upthread: fiesta, fiakre, tiatro
and  kuardicka'u. This last one is a pseudo-lujvo that can easily become a
proper lujvo: ku'arkydicka'u.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

